1
00:00:00,104 --> 00:00:05,442
(Iron Family)

2
00:00:06,894 --> 00:00:10,063
Make sure to keep your daughter
out of my son's sight.

3
00:00:14,552 --> 00:00:15,852
Why aren't you saying anything?

4
00:00:16,461 --> 00:00:17,461
You said you'd do anything.

5
00:00:17,461 --> 00:00:19,292
Get rid of your daughter!

6
00:00:20,861 --> 00:00:22,192
You don't want to?

7
00:00:23,131 --> 00:00:26,032
Can't you do that as her mom?

8
00:00:28,131 --> 00:00:31,001
Then why did you steal my money
in the first place?

9
00:00:33,642 --> 00:00:36,012
I'm so sorry, Ms. Baek.

10
00:00:36,041 --> 00:00:37,582
I'm to blame for everything.

11
00:00:37,881 --> 00:00:39,651
It's all my fault.

12
00:00:45,552 --> 00:00:47,051
Don't make me say more.

13
00:00:49,622 --> 00:00:52,821
I don't want to see you
in the same neighborhood.

14
00:00:53,631 --> 00:00:55,962
Take your whole family...

15
00:00:56,131 --> 00:00:57,902
and leave as soon as possible.

16
00:00:57,902 --> 00:00:59,401
Otherwise,

17
00:01:00,932 --> 00:01:02,501
I'll report you.

18
00:01:05,802 --> 00:01:07,312
Yes, ma'am.

19
00:01:07,671 --> 00:01:09,111
We will.

20
00:01:27,592 --> 00:01:28,961
Mom...

21
00:01:36,641 --> 00:01:38,042
Mom.

22
00:01:38,872 --> 00:01:40,211
Let's go.

23
00:01:40,611 --> 00:01:42,241
I'm sorry, Da Rim.

24
00:01:44,141 --> 00:01:46,512
Let's go, Mom. Come on.

25
00:01:58,191 --> 00:01:59,762
You should go home.

26
00:01:59,962 --> 00:02:02,161
I'll drive you. Come on.

27
00:02:22,952 --> 00:02:24,521
I'm sorry.

28
00:02:27,392 --> 00:02:29,151
What about you two?

29
00:02:29,251 --> 00:02:30,991
Because of me, you two...

30
00:02:34,092 --> 00:02:35,461
Gang Ju.

31
00:02:37,402 --> 00:02:39,401
Get in here this second, you brat!

32
00:02:41,971 --> 00:02:44,341
Seriously? What are you looking at?

33
00:02:44,571 --> 00:02:46,341
Get in here right now!

34
00:02:48,511 --> 00:02:49,912
She's right.

35
00:02:50,541 --> 00:02:52,241
Go to your mom.

36
00:02:53,011 --> 00:02:55,281
Your mom is right here.

37
00:02:56,821 --> 00:02:59,352
Will you be able to get home,
Da Rim?

38
00:02:59,791 --> 00:03:02,222
I'm your mom, darn it!

39
00:03:04,962 --> 00:03:06,831
Hurry inside.

40
00:03:08,561 --> 00:03:11,401
I'm so sorry.

41
00:03:16,902 --> 00:03:18,301
I'm sorry.

42
00:03:22,571 --> 00:03:24,912
You have nothing to be sorry for.

43
00:03:25,511 --> 00:03:27,428
It's all my fault.

44
00:03:27,452 --> 00:03:29,482
Stop helping our family...

45
00:03:30,351 --> 00:03:31,928
and go to your mom.

46
00:03:31,952 --> 00:03:33,892
You are Ms. Baek's son.

47
00:03:34,552 --> 00:03:37,662
You have to take her side
no matter what.

48
00:03:38,761 --> 00:03:40,461
Go, Gang Ju.

49
00:03:41,191 --> 00:03:42,561
Mom.

50
00:03:52,372 --> 00:03:54,472
Are you sure
you're breaking up with her?

51
00:04:02,886 --> 00:04:05,552
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

52
00:04:07,966 --> 00:04:11,061
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

53
00:04:33,911 --> 00:04:35,581
Mom, are you all right?

54
00:04:37,152 --> 00:04:39,791
I'm sorry that I can't drive.

55
00:04:40,791 --> 00:04:42,151
I'm so sorry...

56
00:04:42,892 --> 00:04:45,992
I made you drive
even on a day like this.

57
00:04:50,231 --> 00:04:51,932
What do we do now?

58
00:04:54,971 --> 00:04:57,642
Da Rim, what should we do now?

59
00:04:57,942 --> 00:04:59,911
What are we supposed to do?

60
00:05:06,351 --> 00:05:07,711
Mom.

61
00:05:08,911 --> 00:05:11,481
- Da Rim.
- Mom.

62
00:05:19,632 --> 00:05:20,992
Mom.

63
00:05:35,572 --> 00:05:37,442
Why didn't you go with the family?
Why are you here?

64
00:05:38,082 --> 00:05:40,182
Why did you tell them
to leave the neighborhood?

65
00:05:40,252 --> 00:05:41,481
I said I broke up with her.

66
00:05:41,481 --> 00:05:43,851
They've run a dry cleaner's here
for over 40 years.

67
00:05:43,851 --> 00:05:45,728
How could you kick them out?

68
00:05:45,752 --> 00:05:47,568
Did you really have to do that?

69
00:05:47,592 --> 00:05:50,238
You got your money back.
I gave you the money!

70
00:05:50,262 --> 00:05:52,591
Why do you care
more about her mom, not me?

71
00:05:53,192 --> 00:05:56,331
Do you not mind how
I'm being criticized by everyone?

72
00:05:56,562 --> 00:05:58,438
Is it fine
as long as I have the money?

73
00:05:58,462 --> 00:06:00,702
I can tell
that's how you're feeling.

74
00:06:01,231 --> 00:06:03,502
And I just can't stand it.

75
00:06:03,702 --> 00:06:05,101
Am I wrong?

76
00:06:05,171 --> 00:06:06,541
I feel like...

77
00:06:08,041 --> 00:06:10,541
you abandoned me at the moment.

78
00:06:11,142 --> 00:06:12,711
It really breaks my heart.

79
00:06:13,351 --> 00:06:15,151
It's so upsetting...

80
00:06:15,611 --> 00:06:18,052
and hurtful, Gang Ju.

81
00:06:24,721 --> 00:06:27,091
It's true that I'm a bad son.

82
00:06:27,491 --> 00:06:29,161
I will break up with Da Rim.

83
00:06:30,101 --> 00:06:32,947
I'll make sure to end things
with her.

84
00:06:32,971 --> 00:06:35,302
I promise. Don't report them.

85
00:06:37,942 --> 00:06:39,271
Answer me.

86
00:06:40,312 --> 00:06:43,711
If you report them,
I'll cut ties with you.

87
00:06:43,981 --> 00:06:45,442
Are you threatening me?

88
00:06:45,512 --> 00:06:46,882
Yes.

89
00:06:51,121 --> 00:06:54,267
I'll start setting you up on dates
for marriage tomorrow.

90
00:06:54,291 --> 00:06:55,291
Okay.

91
00:06:55,291 --> 00:06:57,521
- It starts tomorrow.
- Okay.

92
00:06:57,921 --> 00:06:59,608
And they will leave soon.

93
00:06:59,632 --> 00:07:02,562
Don't go near them
before they leave, okay?

94
00:07:02,661 --> 00:07:04,062
I won't.

95
00:07:15,611 --> 00:07:16,911
Please brace yourselves...

96
00:07:17,611 --> 00:07:19,488
and listen to what I say,

97
00:07:19,512 --> 00:07:21,581
Mother, Father.

98
00:07:21,952 --> 00:07:24,952
- What? What is it?
- What's the matter?

99
00:07:27,952 --> 00:07:29,998
Go ahead and say it.

100
00:07:30,022 --> 00:07:31,822
What is it?

101
00:07:31,962 --> 00:07:37,002
I can hardly breathe
because of Bong Hee, Gil Rye.

102
00:07:40,101 --> 00:07:45,148
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

103
00:07:45,172 --> 00:07:47,541
Ms. Baek might report us.

104
00:07:47,983 --> 00:07:49,384
She wants us to leave.

105
00:07:50,183 --> 00:07:51,624
We have to.

106
00:07:52,384 --> 00:07:54,554
We can't blame her
even if she reports us now.

107
00:07:55,594 --> 00:07:57,394
This is unbelievable.

108
00:07:58,194 --> 00:08:00,769
This is driving me crazy.

109
00:08:00,793 --> 00:08:02,634
We have to shut down
the dry cleaner's.

110
00:08:03,204 --> 00:08:05,204
She wants
our whole family to leave...

111
00:08:05,204 --> 00:08:06,773
and stay out of her sight.

112
00:08:07,733 --> 00:08:09,579
Otherwise, she will report us.

113
00:08:09,603 --> 00:08:11,304
Do we have to quit our jobs?

114
00:08:12,274 --> 00:08:14,173
I don't want to quit.

115
00:08:15,313 --> 00:08:16,684
What will you do?

116
00:08:19,913 --> 00:08:23,184
We should put the apartment
and the store on the market.

117
00:08:23,853 --> 00:08:27,793
We have to leave this neighborhood
as soon as possible.

118
00:08:28,824 --> 00:08:30,163
But...

119
00:08:31,024 --> 00:08:33,334
where should we go,
and what should we do?

120
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:37,033
We've lived here for over 40 years.

121
00:08:37,764 --> 00:08:40,233
We still have to go.

122
00:08:40,433 --> 00:08:42,074
We should have a sense of shame.

123
00:08:42,203 --> 00:08:46,103
If she runs into us
in the neighborhood,

124
00:08:46,443 --> 00:08:48,914
she will feel devastated.

125
00:08:49,374 --> 00:08:50,684
Oh, dear.

126
00:08:50,784 --> 00:08:53,284
If I were her,
I'd report us right away.

127
00:08:53,514 --> 00:08:56,083
What do we do with Bong Hee?

128
00:08:56,083 --> 00:08:58,399
What do we do
with our grandchildren?

129
00:08:58,423 --> 00:08:59,723
What?

130
00:09:01,024 --> 00:09:04,163
It's not like
I don't know how to cry.

131
00:09:04,163 --> 00:09:07,363
Don't act like a child
in front of Bong Hee.

132
00:09:08,963 --> 00:09:10,863
Stop crying this instant!

133
00:09:11,463 --> 00:09:13,973
Father, it's all right.

134
00:09:16,234 --> 00:09:17,544
Father.

135
00:09:20,244 --> 00:09:21,544
Father.

136
00:09:23,083 --> 00:09:25,413
Her marriage
with Chairman Ji is over.

137
00:09:25,413 --> 00:09:28,429
It's Chairman Ji's company,
not Ms. Baek's.

138
00:09:28,453 --> 00:09:30,954
I have no reason to quit my job.

139
00:09:31,724 --> 00:09:34,630
Right. You don't have to do that
because of me.

140
00:09:34,654 --> 00:09:36,353
You should keep working.

141
00:09:37,563 --> 00:09:39,024
I'm the problem.

142
00:09:40,093 --> 00:09:41,463
I will...

143
00:09:44,404 --> 00:09:45,934
break up with Gang Ju.

144
00:09:46,604 --> 00:09:48,603
And I'll quit the company.

145
00:09:49,234 --> 00:09:51,603
Actually,
Gang Ju tried to break up with me.

146
00:09:53,443 --> 00:09:55,513
I guess this is why.

147
00:09:59,514 --> 00:10:02,990
Ms. Baek doesn't seem to know
about Grandma and Grandpa.

148
00:10:03,014 --> 00:10:04,723
We should leave
before she finds out.

149
00:10:06,854 --> 00:10:08,493
This is crazy.

150
00:10:09,624 --> 00:10:11,263
I don't know what to do.

151
00:10:14,394 --> 00:10:15,763
Mu Rim.

152
00:10:16,093 --> 00:10:17,934
Just say something.

153
00:10:19,833 --> 00:10:21,174
Mu Rim!

154
00:10:27,744 --> 00:10:29,343
Let's leave this place
as soon as possible.

155
00:10:30,144 --> 00:10:32,220
We made up
for the ten million dollars,

156
00:10:32,244 --> 00:10:34,054
so she won't report us if we move.

157
00:10:34,413 --> 00:10:36,383
We can't let her report
our grandparents...

158
00:10:36,683 --> 00:10:38,324
and have them arrested.

159
00:10:38,583 --> 00:10:40,554
We should close down
the dry cleaner's...

160
00:10:41,154 --> 00:10:42,700
and leave Cheonglyeom-dong.

161
00:10:42,724 --> 00:10:44,294
You guys should keep working though.

162
00:10:44,724 --> 00:10:46,424
I'll keep working as a cop.

163
00:10:46,833 --> 00:10:49,294
We should keep working and earning
to support our family.

164
00:10:51,234 --> 00:10:52,809
I worked so hard to get this job.

165
00:10:52,833 --> 00:10:54,603
Let's close down the store...

166
00:10:54,803 --> 00:10:56,304
and move out.

167
00:10:58,043 --> 00:10:59,574
We just need to leave
this neighborhood.

168
00:11:00,244 --> 00:11:02,314
I'm the only one
who should quit the job.

169
00:11:03,073 --> 00:11:05,444
She's being like that to me
because of Gang Ju.

170
00:11:08,813 --> 00:11:10,223
Let's go home.

171
00:11:11,224 --> 00:11:12,524
Okay.

172
00:11:23,734 --> 00:11:26,103
Do you think
we'll find new tenants soon?

173
00:11:26,364 --> 00:11:29,574
We have to leave
before the word gets out.

174
00:11:30,404 --> 00:11:32,373
Bom's grandmother knows too.

175
00:11:32,443 --> 00:11:33,774
Yes.

176
00:11:34,114 --> 00:11:36,574
Bom's grandmother knows
that we're thieves?

177
00:11:36,813 --> 00:11:38,659
She has such a big mouth.

178
00:11:38,683 --> 00:11:40,154
(Cheonglyeom Villa)

179
00:11:40,154 --> 00:11:42,584
Gosh, this is horrible.

180
00:11:46,261 --> 00:11:48,587
(Junior Staffer Lee Da Rim)

181
00:12:07,178 --> 00:12:09,313
(Letter of Resignation)

182
00:12:09,313 --> 00:12:11,186
(Send)

183
00:12:58,663 --> 00:12:59,870
Hello.

184
00:12:59,894 --> 00:13:02,493
What brings you here so early
in the morning?

185
00:13:03,303 --> 00:13:06,763
Well... I'm putting the apartment
and the store on the market.

186
00:13:06,904 --> 00:13:08,373
Both?

187
00:13:09,433 --> 00:13:10,743
Yes.

188
00:13:10,943 --> 00:13:12,404
Out of the blue?

189
00:13:12,703 --> 00:13:14,973
Does Tae Woong know?

190
00:13:15,673 --> 00:13:17,084
See you.

191
00:13:17,384 --> 00:13:18,684
Bong Hee.

192
00:13:20,913 --> 00:13:21,953
Where to?

193
00:13:21,953 --> 00:13:23,684
Far away from Cheonglyeom-dong.

194
00:13:23,724 --> 00:13:26,753
Mom will find a short-term rental
we can move into right away.

195
00:13:27,593 --> 00:13:29,724
I should return the deposit
with some extra money...

196
00:13:29,724 --> 00:13:31,064
for the apartment and store
right now.

197
00:13:31,693 --> 00:13:32,939
Tae Woong.

198
00:13:32,963 --> 00:13:35,593
You live with Ms. Baek.
Can you keep an eye on her?

199
00:13:35,593 --> 00:13:37,233
See if she reports us or not.

200
00:13:40,034 --> 00:13:41,809
Why won't you answer?

201
00:13:41,833 --> 00:13:45,143
I want to move out of that house.

202
00:13:45,374 --> 00:13:46,474
Gang Ju's back.

203
00:13:46,474 --> 00:13:48,174
I should vacate his room.

204
00:13:50,213 --> 00:13:52,944
Should I just live with you?

205
00:13:54,154 --> 00:13:55,513
In my studio apartment?

206
00:13:55,784 --> 00:13:57,123
Can't I?

207
00:13:58,024 --> 00:14:00,393
What a cheap beginning.

208
00:14:01,793 --> 00:14:03,123
You don't like the idea?

209
00:14:03,364 --> 00:14:04,664
As if I don't.

210
00:14:05,163 --> 00:14:07,794
Lots of couples get disappointed
after they move in together.

211
00:14:08,163 --> 00:14:10,133
I'll dump you
if I don't like your lifestyle.

212
00:14:11,004 --> 00:14:12,334
You do that.

213
00:14:17,374 --> 00:14:19,044
Da Rim handed in her resignation.

214
00:14:21,843 --> 00:14:23,143
What do I do?

215
00:14:23,413 --> 00:14:24,713
Do I approve it?

216
00:14:25,984 --> 00:14:27,484
Send her to another team...

217
00:14:27,484 --> 00:14:28,983
so she can work.

218
00:14:29,413 --> 00:14:31,724
She's too inexperienced
to find another job.

219
00:14:31,724 --> 00:14:33,253
Let her stay and work.

220
00:14:33,693 --> 00:14:35,054
Approve her resignation.

221
00:14:40,186 --> 00:14:42,593
(Online approval)

222
00:14:42,593 --> 00:14:43,715
(Approved by Design Manager)

223
00:14:51,673 --> 00:14:53,074
Should I really approve it?

224
00:14:53,173 --> 00:14:54,490
Approve it.

225
00:14:54,514 --> 00:14:56,914
Did you two break up?

226
00:15:19,858 --> 00:15:21,683
(Approved: Lee Cha Rim,
Approved: Cha Tae Woong)

227
00:15:32,183 --> 00:15:34,324
(Online approval)

228
00:15:35,913 --> 00:15:37,223
You won't approve it?

229
00:15:37,624 --> 00:15:40,893
She was so pleased
to become a regular employee.

230
00:15:54,548 --> 00:15:56,621
(Approved: Lee Cha Rim,
Approved: Cha Tae Woong)

231
00:16:10,453 --> 00:16:13,954
Did Da Rim come back
after quitting her job?

232
00:16:14,994 --> 00:16:17,363
She brought her stuff back.

233
00:16:21,034 --> 00:16:22,833
You should eat
even if you don't feel like it.

234
00:16:22,833 --> 00:16:24,233
Why didn't you?

235
00:16:24,904 --> 00:16:26,480
Shall I reheat your soup?

236
00:16:26,504 --> 00:16:28,274
It doesn't taste good.

237
00:16:28,534 --> 00:16:30,944
I can't taste anything.

238
00:16:32,004 --> 00:16:34,074
Don't act like children.

239
00:16:34,774 --> 00:16:36,774
What's the point of eating?

240
00:16:37,083 --> 00:16:38,383
Grandma.

241
00:16:38,713 --> 00:16:40,960
I can't chew or swallow.

242
00:16:40,984 --> 00:16:42,684
You're not dying.

243
00:16:42,953 --> 00:16:45,684
You have years to go
until you turn 100.

244
00:16:45,823 --> 00:16:48,424
Here. Eat.

245
00:16:48,953 --> 00:16:50,863
Empty your bowls.

246
00:16:53,494 --> 00:16:56,733
I'm too weak to hold a spoon.

247
00:16:57,933 --> 00:17:00,604
Gil Rye. If you don't have
the energy to hold a spoon,

248
00:17:00,604 --> 00:17:03,004
then dying is the only thing
you can do.

249
00:17:03,004 --> 00:17:04,743
Don't even say that.

250
00:17:06,043 --> 00:17:08,073
I need you two to stay strong.

251
00:17:08,073 --> 00:17:09,414
Don't be like this.

252
00:17:10,714 --> 00:17:12,044
Here.

253
00:17:13,014 --> 00:17:14,353
Open wide.

254
00:17:14,984 --> 00:17:17,524
Everything tastes bitter.

255
00:17:17,524 --> 00:17:18,953
Eat anyway.

256
00:17:19,484 --> 00:17:20,994
Come on.

257
00:17:21,954 --> 00:17:23,294
Yes.

258
00:17:26,393 --> 00:17:28,034
You too, Grandpa.

259
00:17:28,434 --> 00:17:30,603
Open your mouth wide.

260
00:17:31,563 --> 00:17:33,680
It's like chewing sand.

261
00:17:33,704 --> 00:17:36,673
I really will feed you sand
if you keep complaining.

262
00:17:36,734 --> 00:17:38,349
You must eat to live.

263
00:17:38,373 --> 00:17:39,950
My arms are aching now.

264
00:17:39,974 --> 00:17:41,814
Eat even if you don't feel like it.

265
00:17:46,313 --> 00:17:49,153
Chew slowly and carefully.
I won't allow leftovers.

266
00:17:50,113 --> 00:17:52,224
Chew thoroughly and slowly.

267
00:17:53,053 --> 00:17:54,353
Take your time.

268
00:18:01,264 --> 00:18:04,834
After this,
take a walk around the block.

269
00:18:04,903 --> 00:18:06,703
I'll pack your things.

270
00:18:06,934 --> 00:18:08,734
Why should we
walk around the block...

271
00:18:08,734 --> 00:18:10,744
we'll move away from?

272
00:18:15,850 --> 00:18:17,113
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

273
00:18:23,414 --> 00:18:24,853
Hae Ja.

274
00:18:26,924 --> 00:18:29,693
They put their apartment
and store on the market.

275
00:18:29,724 --> 00:18:31,623
Are they going through something?

276
00:18:31,793 --> 00:18:33,193
Yes.

277
00:18:33,593 --> 00:18:34,893
Like what?

278
00:18:36,833 --> 00:18:38,564
Do you know something?

279
00:18:40,204 --> 00:18:42,603
They don't deserve to live here.

280
00:18:43,704 --> 00:18:45,443
What does that mean?

281
00:18:46,043 --> 00:18:47,343
When are they leaving?

282
00:18:48,444 --> 00:18:51,814
They'll leave
before they even find new tenants.

283
00:18:52,613 --> 00:18:54,053
It's so odd.

284
00:18:54,053 --> 00:18:56,784
They're acting as if
they're fleeing from creditors...

285
00:18:56,784 --> 00:18:58,324
who are chasing them.

286
00:18:58,784 --> 00:19:01,653
But I know
they're not that kind of people.

287
00:19:02,153 --> 00:19:03,754
Right?

288
00:19:05,093 --> 00:19:07,234
You never know what people are like.

289
00:19:15,103 --> 00:19:16,109
Mother.

290
00:19:16,133 --> 00:19:18,774
My goodness.

291
00:19:23,684 --> 00:19:25,643
I'm not a gossip.

292
00:19:27,754 --> 00:19:29,829
Until the family leaves,

293
00:19:29,853 --> 00:19:32,923
and even after they leave,
you can't tell anyone.

294
00:19:35,353 --> 00:19:36,653
Mother.

295
00:19:54,373 --> 00:19:55,814
You're not leaving?

296
00:19:56,843 --> 00:19:58,314
I will soon.

297
00:19:59,643 --> 00:20:00,953
Where's Tae Woong?

298
00:20:01,454 --> 00:20:03,784
He went to a factory
and will go home from there.

299
00:20:04,454 --> 00:20:05,859
Shall we go home together?

300
00:20:05,883 --> 00:20:07,200
No.

301
00:20:07,224 --> 00:20:08,623
Shall we get dinner?

302
00:20:08,623 --> 00:20:09,953
No.

303
00:20:10,694 --> 00:20:12,339
Shall we have a drink?

304
00:20:12,363 --> 00:20:13,693
No.

305
00:20:15,593 --> 00:20:18,603
You've really changed.

306
00:20:19,133 --> 00:20:21,133
Whenever I suggested something,

307
00:20:21,133 --> 00:20:23,843
you'd jump up and say yes
even before I finished talking.

308
00:20:23,843 --> 00:20:27,173
You never knew how to say "no."

309
00:20:27,843 --> 00:20:29,244
Have you fallen out of love?

310
00:20:29,444 --> 00:20:30,744
Yes.

311
00:20:31,444 --> 00:20:32,913
My word.

312
00:20:33,214 --> 00:20:35,930
Aren't you being a bit too open
about it?

313
00:20:35,954 --> 00:20:38,423
I used to be your number one.

314
00:20:38,853 --> 00:20:40,284
I'm hurt.

315
00:20:42,224 --> 00:20:45,393
My number one is someone else.

316
00:20:46,563 --> 00:20:47,933
Your mom?

317
00:20:48,063 --> 00:20:49,363
No.

318
00:20:49,434 --> 00:20:50,734
Then who?

319
00:20:51,063 --> 00:20:52,279
Ms. Lee Da Rim the secretary?

320
00:20:52,303 --> 00:20:53,633
Yes.

321
00:20:53,833 --> 00:20:55,734
Hey. You said you broke up.

322
00:20:55,734 --> 00:20:56,903
You said you'd break up.

323
00:20:56,903 --> 00:20:58,403
You said you had to break up.

324
00:20:58,403 --> 00:21:02,074
Her family will leave
the neighborhood soon.

325
00:21:02,543 --> 00:21:04,613
Mom threatened to report them...

326
00:21:04,613 --> 00:21:06,183
if they didn't.

327
00:21:08,353 --> 00:21:09,683
Father.

328
00:21:12,754 --> 00:21:14,393
We can't be, can we?

329
00:21:14,623 --> 00:21:15,923
Hey.

330
00:21:16,853 --> 00:21:18,964
Can you send her mother
and grandparents to prison...

331
00:21:18,964 --> 00:21:20,363
and still date her?

332
00:21:29,504 --> 00:21:30,905
Hello.

333
00:21:31,349 --> 00:21:33,790
Hello, ma'am. I'm sorry.

334
00:21:33,790 --> 00:21:35,560
We're closing the place.

335
00:21:35,829 --> 00:21:37,659
We can't take your laundry.

336
00:21:37,659 --> 00:21:39,629
You worked here
for such a long time.

337
00:21:39,629 --> 00:21:41,359
Is something wrong?

338
00:21:42,099 --> 00:21:43,246
I'm sorry.

339
00:21:43,270 --> 00:21:44,770
Okay.

340
00:21:46,069 --> 00:21:47,200
Is there a lot left to do?

341
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,609
I'm glad you're here. I need help.

342
00:21:48,609 --> 00:21:49,916
These are
for the third housing estate.

343
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:51,270
Okay.

344
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:58,080
Da Rim. Your resignation
was approved, right?

345
00:22:01,550 --> 00:22:03,619
Cha Rim, bring those to the car.

346
00:22:03,619 --> 00:22:04,919
Okay. Wait up, Mom.

347
00:22:04,919 --> 00:22:06,290
That's heavy.

348
00:22:12,596 --> 00:22:13,559
(Crosswalk)

349
00:22:13,559 --> 00:22:14,959
I'll see you there.

350
00:22:50,869 --> 00:22:52,069
What's the point?

351
00:22:52,069 --> 00:22:53,365
(Crosswalk)

352
00:22:55,669 --> 00:22:57,010
Still.

353
00:22:58,510 --> 00:23:00,240
As if that'll change anything.

354
00:23:02,349 --> 00:23:03,649
Still.

355
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:07,879
Let's not be clingy.

356
00:23:12,559 --> 00:23:16,596
(Washing, mending)

357
00:23:21,629 --> 00:23:22,869
(Crosswalk)

358
00:24:19,918 --> 00:24:21,629
(We're closing
due to unavoidable circumstances.)

359
00:24:21,629 --> 00:24:22,859
(Thank you
for being long-term customers.)

360
00:24:22,859 --> 00:24:23,889
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

361
00:24:23,889 --> 00:24:25,460
(Business Closed)

362
00:24:49,989 --> 00:24:50,990
(Crosswalk)

363
00:24:50,990 --> 00:24:52,359
I miss you.

364
00:24:53,419 --> 00:24:55,389
Maybe we'll date again
after staying a year apart.

365
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:57,730
How about in ten years?

366
00:24:59,559 --> 00:25:01,260
Eat well and live a good life.

367
00:25:05,700 --> 00:25:06,770
(Crosswalk)

368
00:25:39,599 --> 00:25:40,939
Ms. Lee.

369
00:25:42,770 --> 00:25:44,439
You're a brazen one, aren't you?

370
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:47,285
You're hours late.

371
00:25:47,309 --> 00:25:49,449
Why won't you approve
of my resignation?

372
00:25:50,379 --> 00:25:52,619
- Your resignation?
- Yes.

373
00:25:53,280 --> 00:25:54,820
Is that what you came here for?

374
00:25:57,849 --> 00:25:59,159
Yes.

375
00:26:00,659 --> 00:26:02,129
You're my subordinate...

376
00:26:02,889 --> 00:26:05,800
who resigned without notice,
but you're brazen about it.

377
00:26:06,899 --> 00:26:09,330
I'm only letting it slide
since you've been doing a good job.

378
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,369
Have a drink.

379
00:26:30,750 --> 00:26:32,060
Is it sweet?

380
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:34,659
- Sorry?
- Is it bitter?

381
00:26:36,359 --> 00:26:37,690
I don't know.

382
00:26:37,690 --> 00:26:39,399
Isn't it salty?

383
00:26:41,899 --> 00:26:43,629
I served you my tears.

384
00:26:48,040 --> 00:26:49,510
What a joke.

385
00:26:50,940 --> 00:26:52,340
Was that funny?

386
00:27:03,319 --> 00:27:04,719
Is breaking up...

387
00:27:06,159 --> 00:27:08,830
the only option we have?

388
00:27:09,790 --> 00:27:11,730
Is that really the only way?

389
00:27:12,359 --> 00:27:14,260
Could there be another option...

390
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:17,300
but we're choosing
to break up instead?

391
00:27:18,099 --> 00:27:20,040
Shouldn't we think harder?

392
00:27:20,899 --> 00:27:22,869
Maybe we shouldn't give up.

393
00:27:23,440 --> 00:27:25,109
This is the only way.

394
00:27:26,139 --> 00:27:27,639
Why ask when knowing the answer?

395
00:27:28,849 --> 00:27:30,179
Da Rim.

396
00:27:31,280 --> 00:27:32,719
We should move on,

397
00:27:33,180 --> 00:27:34,919
so stop texting me.

398
00:27:37,550 --> 00:27:40,659
Let's not see each other again.
Don't acknowledge me anymore.

399
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:46,429
Being hung up on each other
won't do us any good.

400
00:27:49,770 --> 00:27:52,240
- Da Rim.
- Don't say my name.

401
00:27:54,169 --> 00:27:55,869
Approve of my resignation.

402
00:28:10,147 --> 00:28:11,190
(Online approval)

403
00:28:11,190 --> 00:28:14,295
(Approved: Lee Cha Rim,
Approved: Cha Tae Woong)

404
00:28:18,290 --> 00:28:19,462
(Approved)

405
00:28:31,169 --> 00:28:33,846
(Online approval,
Approved: Seo Gang Ju)

406
00:28:42,649 --> 00:28:44,020
You should leave first.

407
00:28:44,619 --> 00:28:46,090
You leave first.

408
00:28:52,430 --> 00:28:54,730
- Da Rim.
- You idiot.

409
00:28:55,129 --> 00:28:57,000
I told you not to say my name.

410
00:28:57,899 --> 00:28:59,300
All right.

411
00:29:00,599 --> 00:29:01,969
Ms. Lee.

412
00:29:02,309 --> 00:29:03,446
Junior Staffer Lee.

413
00:29:03,470 --> 00:29:04,939
Seo Gang Ju.

414
00:29:05,379 --> 00:29:07,209
Yes, Da Rim.

415
00:29:08,710 --> 00:29:10,449
Stop saying my name.

416
00:29:14,079 --> 00:29:15,590
Crosswalk.

417
00:29:22,430 --> 00:29:23,830
The Big Dipper.

418
00:29:49,050 --> 00:29:50,389
Gil Rye.

419
00:29:51,419 --> 00:29:52,719
Yes?

420
00:29:53,919 --> 00:29:56,389
What good would it do
to live longer like this?

421
00:29:57,559 --> 00:29:59,960
Only Bong Hee
is being called a thief...

422
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:02,830
and being banished
from the neighborhood.

423
00:30:03,500 --> 00:30:05,416
Da Rim has to end her relationship
with Gang Ju...

424
00:30:05,440 --> 00:30:07,139
when she loves him.

425
00:30:08,540 --> 00:30:10,469
Because of us,

426
00:30:11,240 --> 00:30:14,240
Mu Rim will live his life
worried about being fired.

427
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:17,080
That means he'll end up...

428
00:30:17,250 --> 00:30:18,909
losing Soo Ji too.

429
00:30:19,980 --> 00:30:22,590
His chief will give him the boot.

430
00:30:26,389 --> 00:30:29,065
We haven't done anything
for the children...

431
00:30:29,089 --> 00:30:30,689
rather than be a burden.

432
00:30:32,359 --> 00:30:34,659
The last thing I wanted...

433
00:30:35,369 --> 00:30:38,206
was to grow old like this, Man Deuk.

434
00:30:38,230 --> 00:30:39,969
Same here, Gil Rye.

435
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:43,570
Does going to the afterlife
still scare you?

436
00:30:43,970 --> 00:30:45,310
What?

437
00:30:46,010 --> 00:30:47,909
The time will eventually come,

438
00:30:49,409 --> 00:30:53,149
but don't you want to do something
for the kids before we leave?

439
00:30:54,419 --> 00:30:55,625
What?

440
00:30:55,649 --> 00:30:59,419
Will we only be a burden to Bong Hee
until the day we die?

441
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:02,889
- What?
- We can't let...

442
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:05,800
our grandchildren break up...

443
00:31:05,829 --> 00:31:10,206
with the people they love
because of us.

444
00:31:10,230 --> 00:31:13,199
Da Rim and also Mu Rim.

445
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:15,270
As if we have any power.

446
00:31:16,169 --> 00:31:18,740
What could we do for them?

447
00:31:18,909 --> 00:31:21,010
There's nothing we can do.

448
00:31:21,379 --> 00:31:23,010
Of course, there's something.

449
00:31:23,309 --> 00:31:24,609
What?

450
00:31:30,750 --> 00:31:34,490
- Get me a pen and a piece of paper.
- What?

451
00:31:35,359 --> 00:31:37,689
What for, Gil Rye?

452
00:31:38,899 --> 00:31:40,500
We'll confess to Ms. Baek...

453
00:31:40,629 --> 00:31:43,800
that we're the ones
who stole her money...

454
00:31:43,869 --> 00:31:45,369
and ask for her forgiveness.

455
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:47,446
We should take full responsibility
for everything.

456
00:31:47,470 --> 00:31:50,310
There's nothing
for us to be afraid of.

457
00:31:51,540 --> 00:31:52,840
Gil Rye...

458
00:31:54,139 --> 00:31:55,850
If we die,

459
00:31:56,579 --> 00:31:59,679
Ms. Baek won't report the theft.

460
00:32:01,119 --> 00:32:02,689
If we die,

461
00:32:03,589 --> 00:32:05,550
will she take pity on us...

462
00:32:06,220 --> 00:32:07,659
and choose not to report us?

463
00:32:08,220 --> 00:32:09,590
Will she forgive us?

464
00:32:09,690 --> 00:32:12,730
Just bring me a pen and some paper.

465
00:32:12,760 --> 00:32:14,060
Okay.

466
00:32:14,859 --> 00:32:16,600
This is the only way.

467
00:32:28,389 --> 00:32:30,950
(Police)

468
00:32:35,194 --> 00:32:36,649
(Cheonglyeom Police Station,
Chief Yun Mi Ok)

469
00:32:36,649 --> 00:32:37,649
Chief.

470
00:32:37,649 --> 00:32:40,419
We should find a new dry cleaner's
for our uniforms.

471
00:32:41,520 --> 00:32:43,230
- Why?
- It turns out...

472
00:32:43,230 --> 00:32:46,230
Sergeant Lee Mu Rim's family
is closing down the store.

473
00:32:46,430 --> 00:32:48,736
They will move.
They're leaving Cheonglyeom-dong.

474
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:50,070
What?

475
00:32:51,169 --> 00:32:52,800
That's strange.

476
00:32:53,099 --> 00:32:55,439
They wouldn't leave
the neighborhood so easily.

477
00:32:55,770 --> 00:32:56,839
Oh, right. A few days ago,

478
00:32:56,839 --> 00:32:58,615
we watched some CCTV footage
at the subway station.

479
00:32:58,639 --> 00:33:00,840
Didn't Lieutenant Song Soo Ji
tell you about it?

480
00:33:01,809 --> 00:33:04,879
CCTV footage? What is it about?

481
00:33:23,599 --> 00:33:24,599
What is this?

482
00:33:24,599 --> 00:33:27,199
I think Sergeant Lee's aunt
is hiding money.

483
00:33:40,649 --> 00:33:42,550
Retrieve the videos on the SD card.

484
00:33:43,950 --> 00:33:45,250
Whose is this?

485
00:33:45,919 --> 00:33:48,395
It's from
Sergeant Lee Mu Rim's dashcam.

486
00:33:48,419 --> 00:33:49,730
Keep it to yourself.

487
00:33:50,260 --> 00:33:52,330
Why are you being like this
to your son-in-law?

488
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:55,460
Mu Rim deleted only the videos...

489
00:33:55,460 --> 00:33:57,446
of him and his mom
talking in the car.

490
00:33:57,470 --> 00:33:59,270
People will talk if we have
our department take care of it,

491
00:33:59,270 --> 00:34:00,800
so make sure
to find an outside agency.

492
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:03,470
Find a good one
who can get things done quickly.

493
00:34:03,470 --> 00:34:04,810
Okay?

494
00:34:06,579 --> 00:34:07,879
Chief.

495
00:34:08,510 --> 00:34:12,409
Do you want Lieutenant Song
and Sergeant Lee to split up?

496
00:34:13,349 --> 00:34:16,750
Hey. It will be fine
if there's nothing bad.

497
00:34:17,050 --> 00:34:20,259
I also hope there will be nothing.

498
00:34:43,950 --> 00:34:45,750
Where would you like to go?

499
00:34:48,450 --> 00:34:49,989
Yes?

500
00:34:50,450 --> 00:34:52,165
Well...

501
00:34:52,189 --> 00:34:55,989
We'd like to go to a bridge
over the Han River.

502
00:34:56,390 --> 00:34:58,960
Where would you like to go
after crossing the river?

503
00:35:02,060 --> 00:35:03,400
Well...

504
00:35:04,370 --> 00:35:05,670
Sir.

505
00:35:08,240 --> 00:35:12,339
We will get off
in the middle of the bridge.

506
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:14,610
In the middle of the bridge?

507
00:35:16,749 --> 00:35:18,380
Okay.

508
00:35:29,859 --> 00:35:31,230
Thanks.

509
00:35:38,047 --> 00:35:40,643
(35 Buja-ro, 2 na-gil)

510
00:35:44,398 --> 00:35:47,506
(Sender)

511
00:35:55,419 --> 00:35:56,765
I'm Lee Man Deuk,

512
00:35:56,789 --> 00:35:59,589
the father-in-law of Ko Bong Hee,

513
00:35:59,589 --> 00:36:01,560
who runs Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning.

514
00:36:01,789 --> 00:36:05,159
I'm An Gil Rye, her mother-in-law.

515
00:36:05,459 --> 00:36:08,000
Ms. Baek, we are so sorry.

516
00:36:08,629 --> 00:36:10,770
We've committed a grave sin.

517
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:14,339
Actually, we were the ones
who stole the money.

518
00:36:14,339 --> 00:36:15,739
It was our doing.

519
00:36:16,140 --> 00:36:19,679
We are the ones to blame.

520
00:36:20,010 --> 00:36:22,180
Bong Hee just came with us...

521
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:25,110
because we weren't strong enough
to carry the money.

522
00:36:25,149 --> 00:36:27,225
But she didn't want to go.

523
00:36:27,249 --> 00:36:29,150
It was us who did the whole thing.

524
00:36:35,789 --> 00:36:38,960
We were blinded by money
and told her to go with us.

525
00:36:39,359 --> 00:36:43,429
The only thing Bong Hee did wrong
was not disobeying her in-laws.

526
00:36:44,030 --> 00:36:46,269
Please don't hate
our daughter-in-law.

527
00:36:46,269 --> 00:36:47,569
Bong Hee.

528
00:37:08,689 --> 00:37:10,705
I'm sorry...

529
00:37:10,729 --> 00:37:14,230
that Da Rim regained her sight
and fell in love with your son.

530
00:37:15,030 --> 00:37:19,130
How could one not fall in love
with a man like Gang Ju?

531
00:37:20,800 --> 00:37:24,409
Thanks to your son
whom you raised well,

532
00:37:24,709 --> 00:37:28,486
our family could get some money
and feel happy...

533
00:37:28,510 --> 00:37:30,480
though it was for a short while.

534
00:37:31,350 --> 00:37:34,319
The children didn't do
anything wrong.

535
00:37:41,390 --> 00:37:42,859
Since we have nothing...

536
00:37:42,859 --> 00:37:45,589
but our own lives
with little time left,

537
00:37:45,589 --> 00:37:49,369
we'd like to be punished
by taking our own lives, Ms. Baek.

538
00:37:49,970 --> 00:37:51,470
Can the two of us...

539
00:37:51,470 --> 00:37:54,600
take all the blame and leave?

540
00:37:59,180 --> 00:38:01,709
We will take the blame...

541
00:38:01,709 --> 00:38:05,610
for everything our daughter-in-law
and grandchildren did and leave.

542
00:38:06,149 --> 00:38:10,119
Please forgive us
with a generous heart.

543
00:38:11,249 --> 00:38:14,189
From the thieves
of Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning,

544
00:38:14,189 --> 00:38:17,360
Lee Man Deuk and An Gil Rye.

545
00:38:17,601 --> 00:38:19,260
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

546
00:38:19,260 --> 00:38:20,960
Did you call the police?

547
00:38:21,229 --> 00:38:24,900
What? Yes, I did.

548
00:38:35,864 --> 00:38:37,011
(Bong Hee)

549
00:38:38,429 --> 00:38:39,620
(Missed call)

550
00:38:39,620 --> 00:38:42,973
(Bong Hee)

551
00:38:54,600 --> 00:38:56,969
What if something happens
to Mother and Father?

552
00:38:57,470 --> 00:38:58,799
My gosh.

553
00:38:59,370 --> 00:39:00,940
Where should I go to find them?

554
00:39:01,370 --> 00:39:02,670
Seung Don.

555
00:39:03,339 --> 00:39:05,369
Where do you think...

556
00:39:05,910 --> 00:39:08,509
Mother and Father went
in this cold weather?

557
00:39:09,109 --> 00:39:12,210
Where did they go
to take their own lives?

558
00:39:12,580 --> 00:39:14,250
What should I do?

559
00:39:14,950 --> 00:39:16,866
What do I do?

560
00:39:16,890 --> 00:39:17,966
Mother.

561
00:39:17,990 --> 00:39:20,790
Where should I go?

562
00:39:21,060 --> 00:39:22,389
Seung Don.

563
00:39:22,990 --> 00:39:24,589
Where should I go to find them?

564
00:39:26,800 --> 00:39:28,100
Where?

565
00:39:32,970 --> 00:39:34,740
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

566
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:37,109
(Police)

567
00:40:07,307 --> 00:40:11,893
(Washing)

568
00:40:11,917 --> 00:40:14,243
(Cheonglyeom Villa)

569
00:40:23,692 --> 00:40:27,222
Ma'am, sir, is this where you live?

570
00:40:32,393 --> 00:40:33,832
Aren't you getting off?

571
00:40:37,672 --> 00:40:40,742
I never drop off customers
in the middle of the bridge.

572
00:40:41,373 --> 00:40:44,242
There's no taxi
that takes you to the underworld.

573
00:40:45,043 --> 00:40:47,143
Please hang in there.

574
00:40:47,143 --> 00:40:49,283
Please don't think of anything bad.

575
00:40:58,473 --> 00:41:00,862
(Cheonglyeom Villa)

576
00:41:07,463 --> 00:41:08,763
Bong Hee.

577
00:41:16,536 --> 00:41:18,012
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

578
00:41:22,612 --> 00:41:23,952
Mother, Father.

579
00:41:24,483 --> 00:41:25,983
Are you out of your minds?

580
00:41:26,612 --> 00:41:28,452
What were you thinking?

581
00:41:28,922 --> 00:41:30,792
Do you want us all to just die?

582
00:41:32,822 --> 00:41:35,068
How could you do this to me?

583
00:41:35,092 --> 00:41:38,093
How could you think of leaving me?

584
00:41:39,233 --> 00:41:41,963
We must live or die together.

585
00:41:42,703 --> 00:41:45,003
You can't leave me on my own.

586
00:41:46,902 --> 00:41:49,679
We're sorry, Bong Hee.

587
00:41:49,703 --> 00:41:52,148
Where did you even go?

588
00:41:52,172 --> 00:41:55,213
How could you
even entertain this thought?

589
00:41:55,842 --> 00:41:57,682
Didn't you think about Bong Hee?

590
00:41:57,853 --> 00:42:01,123
We're nothing but a burden to you.

591
00:42:01,123 --> 00:42:02,898
Father...

592
00:42:02,922 --> 00:42:06,829
We thought we'd just drag you
and the kids down.

593
00:42:06,853 --> 00:42:10,292
Why do you think you're a burden?

594
00:42:11,762 --> 00:42:14,533
You don't have to do anything
to be a parent.

595
00:42:15,262 --> 00:42:18,772
Even if you do nothing
but sit next to me,

596
00:42:19,402 --> 00:42:22,073
you're moral support, not a burden.

597
00:42:23,913 --> 00:42:25,343
What more could you do?

598
00:42:25,413 --> 00:42:27,713
Why are you always apologizing?

599
00:42:28,282 --> 00:42:30,142
Old people are still parents.

600
00:42:31,313 --> 00:42:32,852
If you were to die like this,

601
00:42:33,112 --> 00:42:35,222
I'd never survive.

602
00:42:36,222 --> 00:42:38,499
Just being there with me,

603
00:42:38,523 --> 00:42:41,022
just eating with me at the table...

604
00:42:41,123 --> 00:42:43,892
gives me the strength to go on.

605
00:42:44,933 --> 00:42:48,503
- We're so ashamed.
- Yes. We feel terrible.

606
00:42:48,503 --> 00:42:52,073
Mother... Father...

607
00:43:17,963 --> 00:43:20,633
You took your medicine,
so sleep now.

608
00:43:22,503 --> 00:43:24,573
- Oh, dear.
- Let's leave them.

609
00:43:24,933 --> 00:43:27,233
They won't sleep until we leave.

610
00:43:32,572 --> 00:43:34,113
Let's go.

611
00:44:26,992 --> 00:44:29,033
Don't cry.

612
00:44:48,792 --> 00:44:50,054
(Business Closed)

613
00:44:56,362 --> 00:44:57,932
You're strong and brave.

614
00:44:59,192 --> 00:45:00,562
Cheer up.

615
00:45:05,273 --> 00:45:06,772
Who's strong and brave?

616
00:45:08,072 --> 00:45:09,372
Me?

617
00:45:09,572 --> 00:45:11,113
I'm strong and brave?

618
00:45:13,442 --> 00:45:15,443
I'm not.

619
00:45:15,882 --> 00:45:17,613
After my husband died,

620
00:45:18,213 --> 00:45:20,082
I've been pretending
to be strong and brave.

621
00:45:22,583 --> 00:45:25,122
Don't you tell me
to be strong and brave too.

622
00:45:25,393 --> 00:45:28,122
I pretended because I was a mom.

623
00:45:28,893 --> 00:45:30,763
I'm not brave at all.

624
00:45:33,233 --> 00:45:34,602
Get lost.

625
00:45:34,963 --> 00:45:37,062
You be strong and brave and go.

626
00:45:47,043 --> 00:45:48,383
Get lost.

627
00:45:49,043 --> 00:45:50,412
Leave.

628
00:46:32,293 --> 00:46:34,463
Da Rim's grandparents
wrote a letter...

629
00:46:34,862 --> 00:46:36,763
and left it in our mailbox.

630
00:46:36,822 --> 00:46:38,432
Father found it.

631
00:46:38,692 --> 00:46:40,932
They wanted to take the blame...

632
00:46:41,663 --> 00:46:43,903
and pay the price with their lives.

633
00:47:22,773 --> 00:47:24,572
Mom, I'll do that.

634
00:47:24,572 --> 00:47:26,389
- Bring these and follow me.
- Okay.

635
00:47:26,413 --> 00:47:28,113
I'm off to drop off some clothes.

636
00:47:28,213 --> 00:47:29,783
See you later.

637
00:47:30,342 --> 00:47:31,852
See you.

638
00:47:38,623 --> 00:47:39,938
(Washing, mending, dry cleaning)

639
00:47:50,163 --> 00:47:51,503
Is it this one, Mom?

640
00:47:52,503 --> 00:47:53,836
Be quick.

641
00:47:53,860 --> 00:47:56,503
(35 Buja-ro, 2 na-gil)

642
00:48:21,902 --> 00:48:23,479
They'll return my money tomorrow?

643
00:48:23,503 --> 00:48:26,803
Yes. Oh Min Gi's trial ended.
You can pick it up soon.

644
00:48:26,933 --> 00:48:28,602
It was a long wait.

645
00:48:28,703 --> 00:48:30,142
Congratulations.

646
00:48:30,203 --> 00:48:31,619
I'll accompany you.

647
00:48:31,643 --> 00:48:33,173
Okay, thanks.

648
00:48:33,342 --> 00:48:36,059
Will you open an account
at Myungmoon Savings Bank?

649
00:48:36,083 --> 00:48:38,952
Yes. A bank beats any safe.

650
00:48:39,282 --> 00:48:40,883
Let's go straight to the bank.

651
00:48:41,322 --> 00:48:42,653
Okay.

652
00:48:43,282 --> 00:48:44,293
Oh, really?

653
00:48:44,293 --> 00:48:45,692
(Love Capital)

654
00:48:45,692 --> 00:48:46,992
Okay, bye.

655
00:48:48,492 --> 00:48:49,863
What did he say?

656
00:48:50,992 --> 00:48:53,392
She'll take the money
to the bank tomorrow.

657
00:48:53,963 --> 00:48:56,203
She'll go from the police station
to the bank.

658
00:48:56,203 --> 00:48:59,332
We must take it from her
en route as we planned.

659
00:48:59,972 --> 00:49:01,648
- Is everything ready?
- Yes.

660
00:49:01,672 --> 00:49:03,842
We got an unregistered car,
mapped out the route,

661
00:49:03,842 --> 00:49:05,148
and rehearsed as well.

662
00:49:05,172 --> 00:49:07,542
The stowaway brokers
have our fake passports too.

663
00:49:08,143 --> 00:49:10,088
We just have to wait at the dock...

664
00:49:10,112 --> 00:49:11,912
and board the boat on time.

665
00:49:12,413 --> 00:49:13,413
Okay.

666
00:49:13,413 --> 00:49:14,829
Darn Baek Ji Yeon.

667
00:49:14,853 --> 00:49:17,693
We'll stab her in the back,
take her cash, and leave.

668
00:49:18,353 --> 00:49:19,653
- Okay.
- Okay.

669
00:49:26,621 --> 00:49:28,891
(Yun Mi Ok)

670
00:49:30,302 --> 00:49:31,733
Come in.

671
00:49:37,043 --> 00:49:38,343
Chief.

672
00:49:38,543 --> 00:49:40,372
The dashcam footage
has been retrieved.

673
00:49:40,942 --> 00:49:42,683
- Play it.
- Okay.

674
00:49:42,683 --> 00:49:45,253
(Cheonglyeom Police Station,
Chief Yun Mi Ok)

675
00:49:51,322 --> 00:49:52,968
Did you dig up money at Mount Euak?

676
00:49:52,992 --> 00:49:55,522
Why are there wads of cash
under their mattress?

677
00:49:56,422 --> 00:49:58,032
Did Grandma and Grandpa...

678
00:49:58,032 --> 00:50:00,039
- also dig up that money?
- What is this about?

679
00:50:00,063 --> 00:50:01,209
You too?

680
00:50:01,233 --> 00:50:03,108
Your grandparents...

681
00:50:03,132 --> 00:50:05,133
first dug up three million dollars.

682
00:50:05,433 --> 00:50:07,679
The three of us went back...

683
00:50:07,703 --> 00:50:09,542
to get the remaining seven million.

684
00:50:11,713 --> 00:50:14,413
Ko Bong Hee wasn't
the only thief who dug up...

685
00:50:14,413 --> 00:50:16,412
the cash on Mount Euak?

686
00:50:17,913 --> 00:50:19,753
The elderly couple
were in on it too?

687
00:50:21,123 --> 00:50:23,352
Shall I call Sergeant Lee?

688
00:50:23,652 --> 00:50:26,423
They got away with it like that?

689
00:50:27,092 --> 00:50:30,562
He talked back at me
and said his mother was innocent?

690
00:50:30,623 --> 00:50:33,133
- That punk.
- Shall I call him?

691
00:50:33,762 --> 00:50:35,303
He took the day off.

692
00:50:36,802 --> 00:50:38,102
No.

693
00:50:40,072 --> 00:50:41,943
We'll go to him.

694
00:50:50,913 --> 00:50:52,653
Get in quick!

695
00:50:55,382 --> 00:50:57,822
(Police)

696
00:50:57,992 --> 00:50:59,292
Chief.

697
00:50:59,793 --> 00:51:01,093
Chief.

698
00:51:02,492 --> 00:51:07,562
You saw the security footage
from the subway station.

699
00:51:08,203 --> 00:51:09,563
You saw...

700
00:51:09,563 --> 00:51:13,102
how that family paid
suspicious visits to it!

701
00:51:14,802 --> 00:51:16,142
But still,

702
00:51:16,703 --> 00:51:18,372
you said nothing.

703
00:51:18,643 --> 00:51:20,042
You swept it under the rug.

704
00:51:21,483 --> 00:51:23,813
The dashcam footage
from Mu Rim's car...

705
00:51:23,813 --> 00:51:26,412
has your mother-in-law
fully confessing to the crime.

706
00:51:28,782 --> 00:51:30,823
That entire family...

707
00:51:31,123 --> 00:51:32,293
is a bunch of thieves.

708
00:51:32,293 --> 00:51:33,593
Mom!

709
00:51:37,362 --> 00:51:39,492
And you call yourself a detective?

710
00:51:40,663 --> 00:51:42,863
Get your head screwed on straight,
Lieutenant Song.

711
00:51:44,902 --> 00:51:50,641
(Cheonglyeom Police Station)

712
00:51:59,662 --> 00:52:01,948
(Mu Rim)

713
00:52:10,362 --> 00:52:12,092
- What is it?
- Can I at least...

714
00:52:12,092 --> 00:52:14,162
say goodbye
to Da Rim's grandparents?

715
00:52:16,032 --> 00:52:17,809
Is that your way
of going to see her?

716
00:52:17,833 --> 00:52:19,133
Of course not.

717
00:52:40,422 --> 00:52:41,722
Jong Gu.

718
00:52:42,422 --> 00:52:44,263
We're moving.

719
00:52:46,362 --> 00:52:47,703
Do you think...

720
00:52:47,703 --> 00:52:50,803
you can find our new place
on the day of your memorial service?

721
00:52:52,833 --> 00:52:57,042
What if you can't?

722
00:53:01,683 --> 00:53:05,013
Seo Gang Ju hasn't contacted you
after the breakup, has he?

723
00:53:06,753 --> 00:53:08,952
I told him we were moving today.

724
00:53:10,552 --> 00:53:12,153
He's nowhere to be seen.

725
00:53:14,762 --> 00:53:17,338
He's trying desperately hard
to get over you.

726
00:53:17,362 --> 00:53:18,862
So don't be hung up on him either.

727
00:53:18,862 --> 00:53:20,162
Cha Rim.

728
00:53:21,563 --> 00:53:23,363
Stop talking about Gang Ju.

729
00:53:26,103 --> 00:53:27,403
Sure.

730
00:53:42,353 --> 00:53:43,552
Why did I lose my grip?

731
00:53:43,552 --> 00:53:45,092
- Are you all right? Step aside.
- No.

732
00:53:45,092 --> 00:53:46,492
No, it's all right.
You'll cut yourself.

733
00:53:46,492 --> 00:53:48,392
Let me clean this up.

734
00:53:51,233 --> 00:53:52,833
Only grab the big shards.
You'll cut yourself.

735
00:53:52,833 --> 00:53:54,162
Sure.

736
00:53:59,003 --> 00:54:00,332
Mu Rim.

737
00:54:01,773 --> 00:54:03,472
Are you sure...

738
00:54:05,043 --> 00:54:07,872
you're able to continue working
as a police officer?

739
00:54:08,713 --> 00:54:10,843
Are you pretending
that everything's fine...

740
00:54:11,012 --> 00:54:12,883
just to ease our minds?

741
00:54:16,183 --> 00:54:18,053
Mom, I'm asking you.

742
00:54:19,492 --> 00:54:21,323
Don't feel guilty about this.

743
00:54:21,822 --> 00:54:23,562
This was my choice.

744
00:54:23,922 --> 00:54:27,033
I believe
it's right to protect my family,

745
00:54:27,532 --> 00:54:28,738
and I don't regret it.

746
00:54:28,762 --> 00:54:30,102
You...

747
00:54:30,902 --> 00:54:33,673
Are you and Soo Ji all right?

748
00:54:36,203 --> 00:54:37,602
I'll handle it.

749
00:54:38,043 --> 00:54:39,613
What will you handle?

750
00:54:39,873 --> 00:54:41,718
You probably know this,

751
00:54:41,742 --> 00:54:44,353
but Soo Ji and I
were never going to work out.

752
00:54:44,353 --> 00:54:46,753
I tried to be greedy for once,

753
00:54:47,382 --> 00:54:48,883
but I've been struggling.

754
00:54:49,722 --> 00:54:50,999
Mu Rim...

755
00:54:51,023 --> 00:54:52,722
I'm truly all right.

756
00:55:06,831 --> 00:55:08,900
(Police)

757
00:55:17,913 --> 00:55:19,313
It's Unit 202.

758
00:55:19,313 --> 00:55:21,282
Make the arrest
as quiet as possible.

759
00:55:21,282 --> 00:55:22,382
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

760
00:55:22,382 --> 00:55:23,722
Go.

761
00:55:44,472 --> 00:55:45,772
Ms. Yun.

762
00:55:46,143 --> 00:55:48,883
Sergeant Lee, where are you headed?

763
00:55:49,242 --> 00:55:50,843
Are you fleeing?

764
00:55:52,012 --> 00:55:54,013
Are you running away, Ms. Ko?

765
00:55:55,282 --> 00:55:56,983
Why would we run away?

766
00:55:57,483 --> 00:55:59,093
We're only moving.

767
00:55:59,152 --> 00:56:01,463
It's not like we committed a crime.

768
00:56:03,293 --> 00:56:05,293
- Mom!
- Mom!

769
00:56:05,293 --> 00:56:07,032
- Goodness, Bong Hee.
- Bong Hee!

770
00:56:07,032 --> 00:56:08,203
- Bong Hee!
- Oh, no.

771
00:56:08,203 --> 00:56:09,733
Ms. Ko Bong Hee.

772
00:56:09,802 --> 00:56:11,433
You're under arrest...

773
00:56:11,433 --> 00:56:13,872
for grand larceny
regarding Ms. Baek's ten million dollars.

774
00:56:14,302 --> 00:56:16,303
You have the right to an attorney...

775
00:56:16,442 --> 00:56:18,412
and the right to remain silent.

776
00:56:18,442 --> 00:56:20,312
You may challenge the arrest...

777
00:56:20,373 --> 00:56:22,613
and file for damages.

778
00:56:25,313 --> 00:56:26,882
- Mr. Lee Man Deuk.
- Yes?

779
00:56:26,882 --> 00:56:29,152
You're under arrest
for grand larceny.

780
00:56:29,152 --> 00:56:30,453
- Grandpa!
- You're under arrest.

781
00:56:30,453 --> 00:56:31,692
- Father!
- But...

782
00:56:31,692 --> 00:56:33,192
- Ms. An Gil Rye.
- No!

783
00:56:33,192 --> 00:56:35,063
You're under arrest
for grand larceny.

784
00:56:35,063 --> 00:56:36,393
- Mother.
- You're under arrest.

785
00:56:36,393 --> 00:56:37,563
Grandma, Grandpa!

786
00:56:37,563 --> 00:56:39,233
- Father.
- What do we do, Mom?

787
00:56:39,233 --> 00:56:42,303
Chief, what proof do you have
for this arrest?

788
00:56:44,532 --> 00:56:45,972
You punk.

789
00:56:46,532 --> 00:56:48,472
You're not even police.

790
00:56:56,543 --> 00:56:57,912
No...

791
00:56:58,052 --> 00:56:59,412
Mu Rim!

792
00:56:59,652 --> 00:57:00,713
Mu Rim.

793
00:57:00,713 --> 00:57:02,282
- Mu Rim...
- Mu Rim.

794
00:57:02,282 --> 00:57:04,452
- Mu Rim!
- You can't.

795
00:57:08,893 --> 00:57:10,522
Sergeant Lee Mu Rim,

796
00:57:10,563 --> 00:57:11,992
you are under arrest on charges...

797
00:57:11,992 --> 00:57:13,733
of dereliction of duty,
which includes...

798
00:57:14,503 --> 00:57:17,262
impeding an investigation
and evidence tampering.

799
00:57:17,262 --> 00:57:20,378
Mu Rim, no!

800
00:57:20,402 --> 00:57:21,442
My gosh.

801
00:57:21,442 --> 00:57:24,173
Lee Da Rim, Lee Cha Rim,
and Lee Mi Yeon.

802
00:57:24,273 --> 00:57:25,273
The three of you
are being charged...

803
00:57:25,273 --> 00:57:27,673
with the acquisition and possession
of stolen property.

804
00:57:28,713 --> 00:57:30,613
We request
your voluntary cooperation.

805
00:57:31,183 --> 00:57:32,713
We're off to the police station.

806
00:57:33,382 --> 00:57:35,123
You only have to arrest us.

807
00:57:35,123 --> 00:57:37,483
Please don't take them, Ms. Yun.
Ms. Yun, please!

808
00:57:37,483 --> 00:57:39,793
- Ms. Yun!
- The others did nothing wrong,

809
00:57:39,793 --> 00:57:40,922
- Ms. Yun.
- Goodness.

810
00:57:40,922 --> 00:57:43,222
Just arrest us two.

811
00:57:43,222 --> 00:57:46,008
- Grandma, Grandpa!
- No!

812
00:57:46,032 --> 00:57:47,793
- Grandma!
- Mom...

813
00:57:47,793 --> 00:57:50,132
- Mom!
- No!

814
00:57:50,132 --> 00:57:51,873
Mom...

815
00:57:51,873 --> 00:57:53,302
- Mu Rim isn't...
- Go on.

816
00:57:53,302 --> 00:57:55,043
- Mu Rim did nothing wrong.
- Go.

817
00:57:55,043 --> 00:57:58,943
- Mu Rim did nothing wrong.
- Come on.

818
00:58:00,043 --> 00:58:01,513
What am I hearing?

819
00:58:02,865 --> 00:58:06,151
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

820
00:58:07,782 --> 00:58:09,729
They wouldn't commit crimes.

821
00:58:09,753 --> 00:58:11,592
What on earth is going on?

822
00:58:11,592 --> 00:58:14,329
I knew there had to be a reason
for them to move out suddenly.

823
00:58:14,353 --> 00:58:16,423
I thought that if they moved away,
that'd be the end of it.

824
00:58:16,523 --> 00:58:19,162
What's going on, Gi Dung?

825
00:58:20,463 --> 00:58:21,833
Move.

826
00:58:21,833 --> 00:58:23,233
- Goodness.
- My gosh.

827
00:58:23,233 --> 00:58:24,233
Mr. Lee.

828
00:58:24,233 --> 00:58:26,378
Bom, let's go inside.

829
00:58:26,402 --> 00:58:29,273
No. Mr. Lee and Ms. An
are being taken away.

830
00:58:29,273 --> 00:58:31,673
- Mr. Lee!
- Get in. You shouldn't see this.

831
00:58:55,203 --> 00:58:56,533
Hold on.

832
00:58:57,463 --> 00:58:58,772
What...

833
00:58:59,172 --> 00:59:01,003
Did you put them in handcuffs...

834
00:59:01,003 --> 00:59:02,573
when they don't have
the strength to resist?

835
00:59:02,603 --> 00:59:04,318
Isn't this police brutality?

836
00:59:04,342 --> 00:59:05,872
Step aside.

837
00:59:06,043 --> 00:59:07,619
We're conducting official business.

838
00:59:07,643 --> 00:59:10,013
Why are you arresting them?

839
00:59:12,813 --> 00:59:14,283
You'll ride in this van.

840
00:59:15,222 --> 00:59:16,258
Get in.

841
00:59:16,282 --> 00:59:18,329
- Da Rim.
- Go on.

842
00:59:18,353 --> 00:59:19,892
Oh, dear.

843
00:59:21,762 --> 00:59:23,492
Did my mom report this?

844
00:59:25,532 --> 00:59:27,133
Was it my mom?

845
00:59:27,393 --> 00:59:29,163
No, it wasn't her.

846
00:59:29,163 --> 00:59:32,032
Now, go. Please leave!

847
00:59:32,032 --> 00:59:33,632
- Gang Ju...
- Then what?

848
00:59:33,632 --> 00:59:34,672
Come on.

849
00:59:34,672 --> 00:59:36,073
But...

850
00:59:38,072 --> 00:59:40,242
Wait. Chief, hold on.

851
00:59:40,242 --> 00:59:42,183
Why are you arresting them...

852
00:59:42,183 --> 00:59:43,713
when the owner of the money
didn't report it?

853
00:59:43,713 --> 00:59:45,753
My mom knows the truth,
but she didn't report it.

854
00:59:45,753 --> 00:59:48,322
What do you think that means?
She forgave them.

855
00:59:48,322 --> 00:59:50,123
They're moving out due to guilt,

856
00:59:50,123 --> 00:59:51,492
so how could you barge in here...

857
00:59:51,492 --> 00:59:53,123
and arrest the whole family?

858
00:59:53,123 --> 00:59:55,499
That may be true for your mother,

859
00:59:55,523 --> 00:59:56,893
but the police
are making the arrest...

860
00:59:56,893 --> 00:59:58,809
based on evidence
linking them to the theft.

861
00:59:58,833 --> 01:00:01,532
They didn't steal anything.

862
01:00:01,532 --> 01:00:04,163
Mr. Oh and Yang Gil Soon
stole the money.

863
01:00:04,163 --> 01:00:06,546
All they did was dig up
what Yang Gil Soon had buried...

864
01:00:06,570 --> 01:00:08,818
and put every cent of it back.

865
01:00:08,842 --> 01:00:11,873
The entire ten million was buried,
which wasn't an easy feat,

866
01:00:11,873 --> 01:00:13,673
but you still find them guilty?

867
01:00:13,713 --> 01:00:15,358
I see you know a lot
about this case.

868
01:00:15,382 --> 01:00:16,983
Seo Gang Ju, hey!

869
01:00:17,342 --> 01:00:18,683
He doesn't know anything.

870
01:00:18,683 --> 01:00:21,213
He has nothing to do
with our family, okay?

871
01:00:21,213 --> 01:00:24,852
That's not true.
You're right. I know everything.

872
01:00:25,152 --> 01:00:28,522
Even so, I helped them hide the cash
that belonged to my mother.

873
01:00:28,722 --> 01:00:31,192
I waited so that they could make up
for the money they had spent.

874
01:00:31,192 --> 01:00:32,663
They gave back every penny,

875
01:00:32,663 --> 01:00:34,163
and my mom will get
all her money back.

876
01:00:34,163 --> 01:00:35,262
Isn't that enough?

877
01:00:35,262 --> 01:00:37,803
Now, uncuff them. Let them go.

878
01:00:37,862 --> 01:00:40,172
Digging a hole in this cold
almost exhausted me to death,

879
01:00:40,172 --> 01:00:42,373
and all that work can't go to waste.

880
01:00:42,373 --> 01:00:44,448
I can't allow that.

881
01:00:44,472 --> 01:00:46,213
When did you bury it?

882
01:00:46,442 --> 01:00:47,543
Shut your mouth.

883
01:00:47,543 --> 01:00:49,283
On December 31.

884
01:00:49,713 --> 01:00:51,713
It was the day Ms. Ko was arrested.

885
01:00:52,853 --> 01:00:55,358
Did you bury the money
to have Ms. Ko released?

886
01:00:55,382 --> 01:00:56,453
Yes!

887
01:00:56,453 --> 01:00:59,722
There's nothing more to investigate
since all the money showed up.

888
01:00:59,853 --> 01:01:02,022
My mom knows that as well.

889
01:01:02,393 --> 01:01:03,992
- Are you sure?
- Yes!

890
01:01:03,992 --> 01:01:05,963
You buried it to get
Ms. Ko Bong Hee released?

891
01:01:05,963 --> 01:01:07,492
I did.

892
01:01:08,563 --> 01:01:11,633
I know you're Ms. Baek's son.
What's your name?

893
01:01:12,103 --> 01:01:13,349
What?

894
01:01:13,373 --> 01:01:14,718
What's your name?

895
01:01:14,742 --> 01:01:15,742
It's Seo Gang Ju.

896
01:01:15,742 --> 01:01:17,342
- Mr. Seo Gang Ju.
- Yes.

897
01:01:17,342 --> 01:01:20,113
If what you just said is true,

898
01:01:20,242 --> 01:01:23,213
you committed a serious crime
of concealing evidence.

899
01:01:23,313 --> 01:01:25,452
Do you know
that makes you an accomplice?

900
01:01:26,152 --> 01:01:28,159
I need you
to come to the police station.

901
01:01:28,183 --> 01:01:30,559
Fine, let's go. Arrest me too!

902
01:01:30,583 --> 01:01:32,153
No, Gang Ju.

903
01:01:35,422 --> 01:01:37,162
What are you thinking?

904
01:01:37,222 --> 01:01:38,692
I'm an accomplice.

905
01:01:38,692 --> 01:01:40,593
I was in on it too.

906
01:01:40,632 --> 01:01:42,302
I'm with your family.

907
01:01:42,302 --> 01:01:44,873
I went to Mount Euak
with your grandparents.

908
01:01:44,873 --> 01:01:46,909
There was a lot of digging
and burying.

909
01:01:46,933 --> 01:01:49,318
I carried your grandma down
away from the police.

910
01:01:49,342 --> 01:01:52,613
If you're guilty, I am too.
If you're arrested, I should be too.

911
01:01:53,012 --> 01:01:55,042
I should be punished too!

912
01:01:55,213 --> 01:01:56,543
I'm a thief as well!

913
01:01:56,543 --> 01:01:57,643
(Cheonglyeom Dry Cleaning)

914
01:01:57,643 --> 01:01:59,653
Will you keep your mouth shut?

915
01:02:44,339 --> 01:02:46,496
(Iron Family)

916
01:02:46,532 --> 01:02:47,532
This all happened...

917
01:02:47,532 --> 01:02:49,703
because we needed money
for my eye surgery.

918
01:02:49,703 --> 01:02:51,433
Didn't you come here to settle?

919
01:02:51,433 --> 01:02:52,802
Why should I settle?

920
01:02:52,802 --> 01:02:54,873
Mom. I won't break up with Da Rim.

921
01:02:54,873 --> 01:02:56,442
Your threats are powerless now.

922
01:02:56,442 --> 01:02:58,373
The money Gil Soon tried to give us
as he was dying.

923
01:02:58,373 --> 01:02:59,373
Let's get it tomorrow.

924
01:02:59,373 --> 01:03:01,543
I'll announce the sentence
for the theft case...

925
01:03:01,543 --> 01:03:02,883
involving ten million
from Mount Euak.

926
01:03:04,114 --> 01:03:06,049
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)

